I posted a question a couple of days ago on porting LIBTIFF to DEC Alpha.
I received a large number of mail messages giving helpful suggestions.  Thanks
to all of you who took the trouble to reply. I did have a typo in my original
posting: I stated that the Alpha AXP processor has 32-bit long ints.  This is
*incorrect*; thanks to all of those who pointed out that Alpha has 64-bit longs,
not 32-bit.

I found out also that earlier versions of LIBTIFF assume 32-bit longs and
therefore *will not work* on machines that have 64-bit longs. Thanks
to Sam Leffler (author of LIBTIFF) for referring me to v3.3beta002 on sgi.com,
which can handle 64-bit longs, though it does have some compilation errors
which need to be fixed when building LIBTIFF.


