I cannot speak for Digital, but I can describe what OSF ships in its
release.  RSML is simply a set of troff macros that are an expansion on man,
or a set of wrappers around the man macros.  The installation
scripts provided by OSF to our licensees allow them to either incorporate
these added macro definitions directly into the man pages (extra bits, but
each file can be formatted by any man command without the added macros) or
to source the wrappers from a file (a .so line is added to the top of the
source for each man page).  In either case, the pages, if installed
properly, should be formatted correctly my man, nroff -man, or troff -man.
