For OSF/1:

If you want to make backup copies, a more or less standard way is 
to use 'dump'. So, something like

	dump 0uf /dev/rmt0h /usr

will copy your user filesystem to tape. Check the man page for
dump for more info.

Restoring this tape can be done with 'restore'. See also the 
relevant man page. In your OSF doc set there should be a 
manual called 'System Administrators Guide' (or something 
called similar) which explains how to make backups.

For VMS:

I think there exists a command called BACKUP. CAnnot help 
you any further, I don't use VMS from a sysadmin viewpoint.

Wilko

