Isn't rsml coding simply just a set of troff macros. Looking at the top of a
man page file I get:

.\" This manpage source uses rsml coding. 
.so /usr/share/lib/tmac/sml
.so /usr/share/lib/tmac/rsml

Using, for instance, "nroff -man /usr/man/man1/tee.1" will correctly format
the man page. I've tested using ptroff (on a sun) with a man page (+sml/rsml
concatenated) and obtained the correct postscript.

