In article <93286.111429LOPEZJ@EVALUN11.BITNET>, Jose Agustin Lopez Bueno <LOPEZJ@EVALUN11.BITNET> writes:
|>    We bought an external tape unit for our Alpha OSF/1 and OPEN VMS
|>  for make the security system. I am new on OSF/1 system. Coul anybody
|>  answer these questions:
|> 
|>       1) How to mount the unit.
|>       2) Which program must I use for make the copies (cpio, tar, ...)
|>       3) What phylosophy must I use?
|> 
|>  (the model of unit is TLZ06-DA Cassette Tape Drive from DEC)

On OSF/1, you will have to create the device for the TZ06 first. You do that
using the /dev/MAKEDEV script, by specifying "/dev/MAKEDEV tz6". The devices
created will be /dev/rmt0? and /dev/nrmt0? (maybe something other than 0 if you
already have other tape drives on your system).

the /dev/rmt0? will automatically rewind the tape when you write to it,
/dev/nrmt0? will not. The letter after rmt0 specifies what compression you use.
See "man tz" for more details. You have uncompressed format on /dev/rmt0l, for
interchange with other DAT drives, and /dev/rmt0h for compressed format, which
might not be fully interchangeable.

To back up onto tape, you have two possible strategies:

- use tar for full backups "tar cv0 /"
- use dump/rdump for incremental backups

The sys admin manual (on the DEC OSF/1 CD-ROM) has a very well-written tutorial on
backing a system up using dump.
