We have a DEC Alpha/OSF1 on order, and we're interested in
system management software for it.  This could be reasonably-priced
commercial software or really solid free software.  All things
being equal, we'd prefer a commercial product.

Our first priority is some nice backup software.  We need a nice
interface, preferably X-based, that allows our computer operators to
painlessly back up this new system and other UNIX systems on our
network.  It's important that the system keep a directory of what
backup is on what tape.  Our system will come with  4mm DAT drives,
so we won't need a bundled drive-and-software solution.

Our second priority is some account management software.  We
are currently figuring we're going to have to write our own, but
I'm curious as to what's out there.  We add and remove hundreds of
accounts in a year, and need a way to manage groups of accounts (classes)
and mailing aliases.

Our third priority is tape management software.  I don't think
we are going to grow a huge library of user tapes, but it would be
nice if a user could request a tape, have it mounted by the computer
operator, and then have the tape drive assigned to him.

These functions wouldn't have to be bundled together; to get what we
want I suspect we'll end up with three separate packages.  But I'm
interested in what's available.  Please email company/product/contact
info; I will summarize to the net if it seems appropriate.

