> An even easier thing to do is copy /sbin/ls to ~ftp/bin, since the "ls" in
> /sbin *is* statically linked.

In _some_ versions of OSF/1, the /sbin directory has been made largely
shared. If this is the case, then /sbin/ls is a shared-library executable,
and there is a copy of a preloaded libc.so in /loader. If this is the
case on your system, you will need to copy the following files to the
"ftp root" 

	/loader/*	=> ~ftp/var/adm/loader/
	/sbin/loader	=> ~ftp/sbin/loader
	/sbin/ls	=> ~ftp/bin/ls

You won't need libc.so. 


