When I was at Digital, I ran into the problem of swapping in the middle
of an active file system.  Being in the file system group, I modified
ufs_fsck, mount, swapon, newfs to verify that active swap partitions and
filesystems don't overlap each other.  This change was shipped with DEC
OSF/1 V1.3.  For example (not the "in use as swap" message):

/sbin/ufs_fsck /dev/rrz3h
** /dev/rrz3h
/dev/rrz3h overlaps mounted filesystem(s) or an active swap area
Unmount or reboot required before fsck on /dev/rrz3h (start 0 end 199999)
        /dev/rz3b in use as swap (start 103222 end 539381)
/dev/rrz3h overlaps mounted filesystem(s) or an active swap area
Unmount or reboot required before fsck on /dev/rrz3h (start 0 end 199999)
        /dev/rz3a mounted on / (start 0 end 103221)

