Problem with exp-function in DEC-Fortran for AXP/OSF1 (DFAO)

There's a great difference in program-running-time whether using
the Fortran-function exp() or not. If explicitly give a constant
and use the "**"-Operator the runtime is extremly shorter than
using the libraryfunction.

Is anyone out there with an idea how to solve the problem without
changing all of the exp()-calls.

Any help appreciated.

environment, program and results
================================

DEC Alpha 3500 AXP, DEC OSF/1 V1.2, DEC Fortran V3.3-342 for AXP/OSF1

----- program with "manually" build the exponent --------------------
      PROGRAM expman
      REAL   sum
      
      r1 = 5.5  
      DO 10 i=1,200000
      if (i .GT. 1000) r1 = 10.
      sum = 2.7182818**(r1*3.0)
10    CONTINUE
      STOP
      END

----- program with using the exp() ----------------------------------
      PROGRAM expexp
      REAL   sum
      
      r1 = 5.5  
      DO 10 i=1,200000
      if (i .GT. 1000) r1 = 10.
      sum = exp(r1*3.0)
10    CONTINUE
      STOP
      END
	
----- f77-call ------------------------------------------------------
% f77 -o expman expman.f
% f77 -o expexp expexp.f
% f77 ... -v ... =>
/usr/lib/cmplrs/fort/decfort -o /tmp/forAAA026963.o expexp.f 

/usr/bin/cc -o expexp -v /usr/lib/cmplrs/fort/for_main.o \
/tmp/forAAA026963.o -O4 -nocount -lUfor -lfor -lFutil -lm -lots 

/usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/ld -o expexp -G 8 -g0 -O4 -call_shared -nocount \
/usr/lib/cmplrs/cc/crt0.o -count /usr/lib/cmplrs/fort/for_main.o \
/tmp/forAAA026963.o -nocount -lUfor -lfor -lFutil -lm -lots -nocount -lc 

0.0u 0.0s 0:00 84% 0+0k 0+4io 0pf+0w

----- results (time mm:ss) ------------------------------------------

expman 00:10 00:10 00:05 00:05      1.0
expexp 05:06 05:17 02:38 02:35   30.6-31.6 

