RE: the large files.  We have seen performance problems when NuTPU reads in
a large (eg. 10 MB) file.  I've been told that the next release cleans up
its memory management.

Couple of comments:

1. It appears to try to emulate VMS TPU.  We are moving from DEC TPU (Ultrix)
to NuTPU so this can sometimes get in the way.  For instance, I don't like 
its use of ctrl-z.

2. The motif version uses keycodes and not keysym values (forgive me if I'm
murdering this concept but I haven't coded a single X application).  Given 
this, it makes supporting multiple types of x window terminals to be a bear.
Kinda kills the keyboard independence that keysyms are suppose to give you.

BTW: the reason we switched from DEC TPU to NuTPU was the decision to not port
DEC TPU to OSF/1.  It think a/soft will see many more folks in our position
soon.

