In article <SCOLLICK.93Oct6140103@antwrp.enemy.gsfc.nasa.gov>, scollick@antwrp.enemy.gsfc.nasa.gov (Keith Scollick) writes:
|>Has anyone out there setup an anonymous ftp account on their machine?
|>I tried here, but I have a problem with getting the dir command to 
|>work. I get the error:
|>  /bin/ls: Exec format error
|>The ls command by itself is fine, it's just the dir command that seems
|>to be having problems.  Is there a fix to this?  Please respond 
|>if you know.

Use /sbin/ls instead of /usr/bin/ls.  Since ftpd does chroot(2), if use
use the /usr/bin executeables you also need to replicate the shareable
libraries and the loader that allows them to run.  That's probably too 
much effort so it's easier to use the non-shared version in /sbin.

